{
  "message": "Thanks — I can help. To start verification, please give either the full name on the account (case‑sensitive), the email address on file, or your user ID. After you provide one of those, I’ll ask you to confirm any 2 of these on‑file items: date of birth, email, phone number, or address. Which identifier would you like to provide now?"
}

{
  "message": "Thanks — you’re verified. I checked your accounts and cards so we can troubleshoot quickly.",
  "findings": {
    "accounts": [
      {
        "account_label": "Green Account (checking)",
        "account_id": "chk_dm42f8c3a7_green",
        "available_balance": 4827.50
      },
      {
        "account_label": "Blue Account (checking)",
        "account_id": "chk_dm42f8c3a7_blue",
        "available_balance": 1523.75
      }
    ],
    "debit_cards": [
      {
        "account_id": "chk_dm42f8c3a7_green",
        "card_id": "dbc_2f8a7c3d1e9b",
        "last_4": "8472",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "fraud_alert_active": false
      },
      {
        "account_id": "chk_dm42f8c3a7_blue",
        "card_id": "dbc_5e1b9d4f2a8c",
        "last_4": "6183",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "fraud_alert_active": false
      }
    ],
    "recent_activity_note": "I see several posted ATM withdrawals today from your Green account (multiple banks). That can sometimes hit per-day ATM limits or trigger terminal issues at non-Rho ATMs."
  },
  "explanation": "All of the cards on your two accounts show ACTIVE and no fraud blocks in our system. Common reasons for declines at non‑Rho ATMs are: the ATM operator's own per‑transaction limit, the machine being flagged (terminal issue), or your card hitting a daily ATM limit. We can take actions that may help right now.",
  "options_and_next_steps": [
    "I can request a temporary ATM limit increase (24 hours) on either your Green or Blue debit card. Temporary increases are allowed if account/card eligibility is met and the boost can be up to 150% of the current limit. Note: third‑party ATM operator limits cannot be changed by us.",
    "If you prefer not to change limits, you can try a Rho‑Bank ATM (no operator issues) or try a different bank ATM that’s bank‑branded (sometimes independent ATMs decline more).",
    "If someone nearby can withdraw for you, you could send them funds via EveryonePay — I can explain that flow if useful."
  ],
  "ask": "How much cash do you need right now, and which card would you like me to request a temporary ATM limit increase for (Green last4 8472 or Blue last4 6183)? Reply with the amount and the card (for example: “$200 on Green”). If you’d rather try a Rho‑Bank ATM or send money to someone nearby, say that instead."
}

{
  "message": "I can look up Sofia’s Light Green (teen) account and card for you. I’ll check: card status, the account’s daily ATM limit and how much’s been used today, and any parental controls that might be blocking ATM withdrawals. If eligible I can also request a temporary ATM limit increase for her card.",
  "what_i_need_from_you_now": "Please reply with Sofia’s full name exactly as listed on her account (case‑sensitive) or her email/user id, and confirm that you (as her parent/guardian) authorize me to access her account and, if needed, request a temporary ATM limit increase or adjust parental controls on her behalf. Example reply: \"Sofia Maria Martinez, authorize\" or provide her email and \"authorize\".",
  "notes": [
    "Light Green (teen) accounts commonly have a $150/day ATM limit — that often causes declines.",
    "If you authorize changes, I’ll perform the lookup and tell you what actions are available (and any eligibility limits).",
    "If you’d rather not give her exact account name here, you can also check her settings quickly in the Rho mobile app where parental controls and limits are shown."
  ]
}

{
  "message": "I tried to request a temporary increase for Sofia, but Light Green (teen) accounts have a fixed $150/day ATM limit that we cannot raise.",
  "details": {
    "card_id": "dbc_9c3e7f1b5d2a",
    "current_daily_atm_limit": 150,
    "attempted_increase": 225,
    "result": "Denied — teen account limits are fixed by policy and cannot be increased by agents."
  },
  "recommendations": [
    "You can transfer funds from your Green account (or Blue) to Sofia using EveryonePay or an internal transfer so she can withdraw up to $150 today and still have funds remaining for future days.",
    "Or you can withdraw the needed cash from your Green card (it has an $825 temporary limit now) and give Sofia the cash or pay the tow truck directly.",
    "If you want, I can walk you through sending an EveryonePay to a nearby friend/family member to withdraw the cash for you."
  ],
  "ask": "Which would you like to do now — (A) transfer money to Sofia, (B) withdraw from your Green card (use the $825 limit), or (C) send funds to someone nearby via EveryonePay? Reply with A, B, or C."
}
